gly-good-at-distinguishing-between-human-emotions-even-some-negative-ones-180989329/</guid></item><item><title>一只“极其罕见”的半雄半雌鸟暂时在芝加哥郊外定居</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-extremely-rare-half-male-half-female-bird-temporarily-took-up-residence-outside-of-chicago-180989377/</link><description>长相不寻常的bobolink是所谓的双侧雌雄同体动物。这只鸟的行为像雄性，最终追求配偶并抚养雏鸟</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-extremely-rare-half-male-half-female-bird-temporarily-took-up-residence-outside-of-chicago-180989377/</guid></item><item><title>这些“极其罕见”的 17 世纪绘画保存得令人惊讶。现在它们是近一个世纪以来首次展出</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/extremely-rare-artworks-from-17th-century-drawing-book-were-astonishingly-well-preserved-now-they-are-on-display-for-first-time-in-nearly-century-180989374/</link><description>阿姆斯特丹国家博物馆获得了这本图画书，其中的作品出自 17 世纪荷兰著名画家 Rombout Uylenburgh 之手，他的遗产后来陷入了默默无闻</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:00:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/extremely-rare-artworks-from-17th-century-drawing-book-were-astonishingly-well-preserved-now-they-are-on-display-for-first-time-in-nearly-century-180989374/</guid></item><item><title>美国宇航局资助的救援坠落太空望远镜的任务正式以失败告终</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-funded-mission-to-rescue-a-falling-space-telescope-officially-ends-in-failure-180989376/</link><description>商业 LINK 航天器本应为 NASA 的雨燕天文台提供动力，将其推入更高的轨道以延长其寿命。但推出后，LINK 遇到了一些问题。雨燕预计将在今年年底重新进入地球大气层并燃烧殆尽</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:35:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasa-funded-mission-to-rescue-a-falling-space-telescope-officially-ends-in-failure-180989376/</guid></item><item><title>贝叶挂毯应该如何结束？一项新的竞赛邀请孩子们重新想象其缺失的最终面板</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-should-the-bayeux-tapestry-end-new-a-competition-invites-childresn-to-reimagine-its-missing-final-panel-180989366/</link><description>一些历史学家认为这幅 230 英尺长的艺术品缺少最后一块面板，该面板可能曾经描绘过征服者威廉的加冕典礼。当挂毯在伦敦展出时，学生们将起草自己的结局</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:50:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-should-the-bayeux-tapestry-end-new-a-competition-invites-childresn-to-reimagine-its-missing-final-panel-180989366/</guid></item><item><title>独角鲸具有标志性的直螺旋獠牙。科学家刚刚揭开了一些引人注目的结构秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/narwhals-sport-iconic-straight-spiraled-tusks-scientists-just-uncovered-some-of-the-eye-catching-features-structural-secrets-180989368/</link><description>北极鲸是唯一已知的长着直牙的动物，而且牙总是向左扭曲。新的研究表明，内层向右扭曲，相反的螺旋提供强度并帮助象牙笔直生长</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:11:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/narwhals-sport-iconic-straight-spiraled-tusks-scientists-just-uncovered-some-of-the-eye-catching-features-structural-secrets-180989368/</guid></item><item><title>奥地利的建筑工程在足球场下发现了罗马时代的万人坑。新研究表明男性的敌人瞄准了他们的“敏感区域”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-in-austria-revealed-roman-era-mass-grave-beneath-soccer-field-new-research-suggests-that-the-mens-enemies-targeted-their-sensitive-areas-180989372/</link><description>没有书面记录提及在这些人死亡时维也纳这一特定地区发生过战斗。但他们受伤的残酷性质，特别是骨盆区域，表明这些人死在战场上</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:06:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/construction-in-austria-revealed-roman-era-mass-grave-beneath-soccer-field-new-research-suggests-that-the-mens-enemies-targeted-their-sensitive-areas-180989372/</guid></item><item><title>爱尔兰的“凯里牛”骨头实际上是野猪和熊，改变了岛上农业的故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/irelands-kerry-cow-bones-are-actually-wild-boar-and-bear-shaking-up-the-story-of-farmings-arrival-on-the-island-180989371/</link><description>这些骨头是 30 多年前在丁格尔半岛发现的，但科学家最近决定重新审视它们，这次是使用现代技术</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:40:44 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/irelands-kerry-cow-bones-are-actually-wild-boar-and-bear-shaking-up-the-story-of-farmings-arrival-on-the-island-180989371/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家发现了数千个完整的古代人类大脑。科学家表示他们已经弄清楚为什么器官不会总是腐烂</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-have-found-thousands-of-intact-ancient-human-brains-scientists-say-theyve-figured-out-why-the-organs-dont-always-rot-180989370/</link><description>一项新研究表明，在适当的条件下（潮湿和缺氧），导致组织分解的化学反应可能会产生相反的效果</description><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-have-found-thousands-of-intact-ancient-human-brains-scientists-say-theyve-figured-out-why-the-organs-dont-always-rot-180989370/</guid></item><item><title>为什么昆虫不生活在海洋中？由于潜入深海的苍蝇幼虫，科学家们刚刚排除了一种可能的解释</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-dont-insects-live-in-the-ocean-scientists-just-ruled-out-one-possible-explanation-thanks-to-deep-diving-fly-larvae-180989348/</link><description>研究人员认为昆虫可能不会生活在那里，因为它们的呼吸系统会因水压而崩溃。但东非的某些苍蝇幼虫每天都会在含有弹性蛋白质的强大气囊的帮助下前往马拉维湖的底部</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:52:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-dont-insects-live-in-the-ocean-scientists-just-ruled-out-one-possible-explanation-thanks-to-deep-diving-fly-larvae-180989348/</guid></item><item><title>波兰乡村一座 182 英尺高的雕像现在是全欧洲最高的圣母玛利亚雕像。当地人希望它能成为旅游胜地</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-towering-182-feet-tall-statue-in-rural-poland-now-tallest-virgin-mary-in-europe-locals-hope-it-will-become-tourist-destination-180989364/</link><description>这座纪念耶稣母亲的钢铁和混凝土纪念碑位于距离华沙约 100 英里的乡村科诺托皮 (Konotopie)</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:07:11 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-towering-182-feet-tall-statue-in-rural-poland-now-tallest-virgin-mary-in-europe-locals-hope-it-will-become-tourist-destination-180989364/</guid></item><item><title>为什么有些章鱼如此聪明？答案可能在于一种前所未见的突变，可以帮助他们准确地构建蛋白质</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-are-some-octopuses-so-smart-the-answer-might-lie-in-a-never-before-seen-mutation-that-helps-them-accurately-build-proteins-180989319/</link><description>科学家们在某些章鱼的核糖体 RNA 中发现了一个奇怪的特征，这种分子可以为细胞蛋白质工厂创建 3D 支架。它只在浅水生物中发现，这些生物具有扩展的神经系统并且可以做出复杂的行为</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:00:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-are-some-octopuses-so-smart-the-answer-might-lie-in-a-never-before-seen-mutation-that-helps-them-accurately-build-proteins-180989319/</guid></item><item><title>巴西近一个世纪以来首次城市黄热病爆发可能是由一个令人惊讶的罪魁祸首造成的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brazils-first-urban-yellow-fever-outbreak-in-nearly-a-century-may-have-been-fueled-by-a-surprising-culprit-180989363/</link><description>众所周知，极端潮湿的环境有助于传播黄热病等蚊媒疾病。但根据计算机模拟，研究人员怀疑严重干旱可能是导致这个南美国家最近致命流行病的原因</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brazils-first-urban-yellow-fever-outbreak-in-nearly-a-century-may-have-been-fueled-by-a-surprising-culprit-180989363/</guid></item><item><title>您现在可以在大都会艺术博物馆看到现存最古老的《奥德赛》副本之一</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/you-can-now-see-one-of-oldest-surviving-copies-of-the-odyssey-at-metropolitan-museum-of-art-180989360/</link><description>纸莎草碎片包含三行，这些行在荷马史诗的标准现代翻译中没有出现</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:19:26 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/you-can-now-see-one-of-oldest-surviving-copies-of-the-odyssey-at-metropolitan-museum-of-art-180989360/</guid></item><item><title>猴子养宠物吗？研究发现灵长类动物与其他动物物种（从老鼠到鹿）之间存在广泛的相互作用</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/do-monkeys-keep-pets-study-finds-widespread-primate-interactions-with-other-animal-species-from-mice-to-deer-180989356/</link><description>科学家表示，这种社会行为可能揭示了人类饲养宠物特征的进化根源，从照顾到宽容和好奇心。但这和养猫养狗不一样</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:22:41 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/do-monkeys-keep-pets-study-finds-widespread-primate-interactions-with-other-animal-species-from-mice-to-deer-180989356/</guid></item><item><title>这种新批准的嗜睡症药物是第一个针对睡眠障碍的根本原因而不是其症状的药物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-newly-approved-narcolepsy-drug-is-the-first-to-target-the-sleep-disorders-root-cause-rather-than-its-symptoms-180989362/</link><description>美国食品和药物管理局刚刚批准了一种名为 Orzeyful 的药物，用于治疗成人 1 型发作性睡病。这种情况是由产生食欲素的脑细胞丧失引起的，食欲素是调节睡眠-觉醒周期的重要化学物质</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:18:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-newly-approved-narcolepsy-drug-is-the-first-to-target-the-sleep-disorders-root-cause-rather-than-its-symptoms-180989362/</guid></item><item><title>拯救一棵在革命战争中幸存下来的 300 岁古树的斗争</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-fight-to-save-300-year-old-tree-that-survived-revolutionary-war-battle-180989357/</link><description>树木学家正在努力保护南卡罗来纳州尤托斯普林斯战场公园 (Eutaw Springs Battlefield Park) 的 45 英尺高的活橡树。这棵历史树在 50 年前的一次雷击中受损</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:50:28 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-fight-to-save-300-year-old-tree-that-survived-revolutionary-war-battle-180989357/</guid></item><item><title>窃贼潜入博物馆并在夜间将其带走几个月后，在一个纸板箱中发现了价值 1000 万美元的被盗杰作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stolen-masterpieces-worth-10-million-discovered-in-a-cardboard-box-months-after-thieves-snuck-into-a-museum-and-whisked-them-away-into-the-night-180989358/</link><description>塞尚、雷诺阿和马蒂斯的艺术作品在今年早些时候的一次三分钟抢劫中消失了。现在，警方逮捕了与意大利北部入室盗窃案有关的五名嫌疑人</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:24:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stolen-masterpieces-worth-10-million-discovered-in-a-cardboard-box-months-after-thieves-snuck-into-a-museum-and-whisked-them-away-into-the-night-180989358/</guid></item></channel></rss>